<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Freetown</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Freetown is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a>, on the Sierra Leone Peninsula at the mouth of the Sierra Leone River. It was founded in 1792 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone-company">Sierra Leone Company</a> as a settlement for freed slaves, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-loyalists">Black Loyalists</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a>, after the earlier Province of Freedom collapsed. It became the capital of the British colony in 1808 and a base for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>'s campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/freetown.jpg" alt="Freetown" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Hond · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Freetown-aerialview.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
